WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:01.790
Hey, David, are you.

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:06.450
Now ready to talk about who Joe Biden will
likely select as his vise presidential running

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.450
mate.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.450
Yes, I am.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.440
I've made it a point not to put the cart before
the horse.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.110
So back in 2017 and 2018, before the midterms,
people would say, what are you thinking about

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.020
Democratic primary presidential candidates?

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.950
And I said, I'm thinking about the midterm.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.420
I'll talk about that later when we still had
a primary going on.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.490
People would call into the show or ask me
during livestreams.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:32.899
Who do you see as the best running mate for
whoever is the nominee?

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.860
And we didn't know who the nominee was going
to be.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.589
And I said, let's take it one step at a time.

00:00:36.589 --> 00:00:40.890
So I'm going to answer the question as it's
asked, which is who do I

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.329
believe is likely?

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:48.450
I think right now the top three possibilities
for Joe Biden, given that he said he would

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.940
be selecting that he would be selecting a
woman as his running mate would be in no particular

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.940
order.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:00.299
Kamala Harris, Amy Klobuchar and I would like
to think Elizabeth Warren now I've read conflicting

00:01:00.299 --> 00:01:06.410
things about the likelihood of a possible
Warren running mate selection.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:12.550
And a number of opinions are she would be
likely to be doing something in Biden's administration,

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.690
but not V.P.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.870
We've heard about Warren possibly as treasury
secretary.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:19.390
That would be quite a change from Stephen
Manoogian.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.170
We've heard about Warren possibly as secretary
of state.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.630
A lot is being floated around.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:28.180
So in no particular order, I think the most
likely or Carmela, Warren and Amy.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.900
Now, that being said, there's some other interesting
names that are that are increasingly being

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:32.900
discussed.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:38.120
Gretchen Whitmer, the governor of Michigan,
is increasingly being being discussed.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.240
Her response to Corona virus has been notable.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.800
I don't know whether to call it good or bad.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.330
You know, a lot of the responses that are
called really good are in states with a ton

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.330
of cases.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.330
New York is an example.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:50.630
Michigan is an example.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.960
The argument would be, well, they'd be even
worse off if it weren't for these governors.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.700
In any case, because Trump has been going
after her.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.820
Gretchen Whitmer is very much in the public
eye.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.560
Michelle Obama has been floated around.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.560
I don't see it.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.150
I just don't see it at all.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:13.890
Stacey Abrams, who fell short of winning the
2018 Georgia gubernatorial election.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.230
To Brian Kemp.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.820
He was both running in that election and running
the election as secretary of state.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.820
Interesting, right?

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.260
Stacey Abrams lost.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.740
She's being mentioned as a possible Biden
running mate.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.050
I would be shocked if it's Stacey Abrams.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.870
It just doesn't feel like that's the direction
it's going.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.750
And then a few people have e-mailed me saying
that Bernie surrogate Nina Turner should be

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.150
selected by Joe Biden.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.010
I see zero chance of that.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.910
I just don't see any way that that becomes
a reality.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.780
Tammy Duckworth has been mentioned.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:49.170
I think that would be an interesting pick,
although it seems less likely than Amy, Kamala,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.360
maybe Warren.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.940
And then also the ideas has been increasingly
floated.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.390
Some people are talking about Andrew Cuomo,
governor of New York, should replace Biden

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.040
as the presidential candidate.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.090
I don't see how you make that happen again
unless something incredibly serious happened

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.090
to Joe Biden.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.380
I don't see that.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:11.360
But the idea of drafting Cuomo as V.P., of
course, Biden would have to go back on having

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.630
said he was going to pick a woman.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.020
I think that would look really bad.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:20.510
And I don't see Biden doing it unless circumstances
that I can't even imagine come to fruition.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.170
But that's been mentioned as well.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:28.819
Abandon his call to select a woman and go
with Andrew Cuomo, very high favourability

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:32.770
and sort of in the public eye as a result
of his coronavirus handling.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.090
Again, New York with a crazy amount of cases.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:41.410
CUOMO Communicating well, communicating almost
daily and turning things around and getting

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.290
getting to the peak much faster than many
other states.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.290
It's an idea.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.900
It probably would be a helpful one in a vacuum.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.349
But going back on his word about a female
running mate may have been a problem.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:53.349
This

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:58.460
is why many people say you never want to commit
to any identity boxes being checked by your

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.349
candidate because then you're artificially
limiting yourself.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:07.890
Biden's calculation was saying he would select
a woman, would help him more than it would

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.580
potentially limit his choices and do damage
in the future.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.520
So if you said, David, you've got a bet.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.440
Who is it going to be?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.650
I. I'm leaning towards Kamala.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.940
I'm leaning towards Kamala.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.470
And this is not an endorsement of Kamala in
any way.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:26.730
But if you said I have to bet on only one,
I would guess Kamala Harris, I think we will

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.510
soon know.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:33.190
Biden letting Bernie know several weeks ago
that he was starting to vet vise presidential

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.190
candidates.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.710
And we will all know very, very soon we have
it.

